      "results": [
        {
          "ruleId": "review-note",
          "ruleIndex": 0,
          "kind": "informational",
          "level": "none",
          "guid": "ms5td90fgyzhh925",
          "message": {
            "text": "blocked_reason belongs in ticketEqualForRender even though the bug was invisible in production — this function is the gate on whether a per-row effect ever fires.\n\nHS-9336 added the .blocked border but never registered the field here. It appeared to work: every server round-trip also bumps updatedat, which is on the list, so the signal fired and the border repainted for the wrong reason. optimisticUpdate has no such cover — it merges a bare Partial<Ticket> into the existing object, so a { blockedreason }-only patch leaves updated_at untouched and the row keeps a stale border.\n\nThe new unit tests isolate this deliberately: makeTicket holds updatedat fixed, so the assertions exercise a blockedreason-only change. They failed on BOTH the list row and the column card before this line was added — which is how the second half of HS-9487 surfaced at all.\n\nStanding rule for the next indicator: the field it reads goes on this list.\n",
            "markdown": "`blocked_reason` belongs in `ticketEqualForRender` even though the bug was invisible in production — this function is the gate on whether a per-row effect ever fires.\n\nHS-9336 added the `.blocked` border but never registered the field here. It appeared to work: every server round-trip also bumps `updated_at`, which is on the list, so the signal fired and the border repainted for the wrong reason. `optimisticUpdate` has no such cover — it merges a bare `Partial<Ticket>` into the existing object, so a `{ blocked_reason }`-only patch leaves `updated_at` untouched and the row keeps a stale border.\n\nThe new unit tests isolate this deliberately: `makeTicket` holds `updated_at` fixed, so the assertions exercise a `blocked_reason`-only change. They failed on BOTH the list row and the column card before this line was added — which is how the second half of HS-9487 surfaced at all.\n\nStanding rule for the next indicator: the field it reads goes on this list.\n"
          },
          "locations": [
            {
              "physicalLocation": {
                "artifactLocation": {
                  "uri": "src/client/ticketsStore.ts"
                },
                "region": {
                  "startLine": 113,
                  "endLine": 126,
                  "snippet": {
                    "text": "    // HS-9045 — the \"merge pending\" row indicator reads this, so a change to it\n    // (worker sets it / owner clears it on integration) must fire the per-row\n    // signal even when nothing else changed.\n    && a.pending_integration === b.pending_integration\n    // HS-9107 — the merge-pending badge's Review action reads the branch.\n    && a.integration_branch === b.integration_branch\n    // HS-9487 — the `.blocked` row/card border (docs/116 §116.3) reads this, so a\n    // change to it has to fire the per-row signal. Omitted when HS-9336 added the\n    // border; a server round-trip happened to repaint anyway because it also bumps\n    // `updated_at`, but `optimisticUpdate` merges a bare patch without touching\n    // `updated_at`, so a blocked_reason-only patch would have left a stale border.\n    && a.blocked_reason === b.blocked_reason;\n}\n"
                  }
                }
              }
            }
          ],
          "properties": {
            "tags": [
              "rationale"
            ]
          },
          "workItemUris": [
            "HS-9487"
          ],
